ited_by_count":55,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10924-007-0072-5","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I1312222531","I4210140558"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Journal of Polymers and the Environment","last_updated":"2026-11-07T11:25:07.637180","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10924-007-0072-5","openalex_topics":["T10513","T10610","T10661"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10513","pub_date":"2007-10-01","study_type":"article","title":"Cellulose Fiber/Bentonite Clay/Biodegradable Thermoplastic Composites","type":"article","work_id":"W2139213567","year":2007},{"abstract":"","author_count":3,"author_ids":["A5032295889","A5060882878","A5113702793"],"author_institution_ids":["I4210140558"],"authors":[{"id":"A5032295889","name":"Gregory M. Glenn"},{"id":"A5113702793","name":"Syed H. Imam"},{"id":"A5060882878","name":"William John Orts"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":22,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1557/mrs.2011.205","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I4210140558"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"MRS Bulletin","last_updated":"2026-11-08T12:12:28.789561","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1557/mrs.2011.205","openalex_topics":["T10513","T10661","T12628"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10661","pub_date":"2011-09-01","study_type":"article","title":"Starch-based foam composite materials: Processing and bioproducts","type":"article","work_id":"W2317810974","year":2011},{"abstract":"","author_count":4,"author_ids":["A5008317231","A5032295889","A5060882878","A5111664591"],"author_institution_ids":["I1312222531","I4210140558"],"authors":[{"id":"A5111664591","name":"Randal L. Shogren"},{"id":"A5008317231","name":"Delilah F. Wood"},{"id":"A5060882878","name":"William John Orts"},{"id":"A5032295889","name":"Gregory M. Glenn"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":false,"cited_by_count":263,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spc.2019.04.007","domain_tags":["soil_and_agriculture"],"facet_tags":["matrix:soil_and_agriculture"],"institution_ids":["I1312222531","I4210140558"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Sustainable Production and Consumption","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spc.2019.04.007","openalex_topics":["T10513","T10661","T13240"],"plastic_related":false,"plastic_tier":"","primary_topic":"T10661","pub_date":"2019-04-18","study_type":"article","title":"Plant-based materials and transitioning to a circular economy","type":"article","work_id":"W2936299167","year":2019},{"abstract":"Microplastic pollution is a growing concern, and natural materials are being increasingly sought as plastic alternatives. Semisynthetic biopolymers occupy a grey area between natural and synthetic materials and are often presented as green alternatives to conventional plastic. They can be water-soluble or insoluble, and are ubiquitous in commercial products as thickeners, films, filters, viscosity modifiers and coatings. This work compares the mineralization kinetics of cellulose, guar and several of their commercialized derivatives using a simple pseudo first-order kinetic model to extrapolate half-lives and lifetimes, while identifying the levers that influence the mineralization rates of these ubiquitous materials. Industrial composting rates were consistently faster than those of wastewater. While partially substituted biopolymers exhibited measurable degradation, kinetic analysis revealed this effect could be entirely accounted for by the fraction of unsubstituted biopolymer. Surprisingly, the initial rates of highly substituted biopolymers exhibited persistence on par with conventional plastics over the experimental durations studied.","author_count":8,"author_ids":["A5020840113","A5032295889","A5041563613","A5060882878","A5067823186","A5093674921","A5111722036"],"author_institution_ids":["I4210140558"],"authors":[{"id":"A5020840113","name":"William Hart\u2010Cooper"},{"id":"A5093674921","name":"Nabeel Kalla"},{"id":"A5111722036","name":"Artur K. Klamczynski"},{"id":"A5067823186","name":"Lennard F. Torres"},{"id":"A5032295889","name":"Gregory M. Glenn"},{"id":"A5041563613","name":"Julia C. Cunniffe"},{"id":"","name":"Kaj Johnson"},{"id":"A5060882878","name":"William John Orts"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":8,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmats.2023.1331308","domain_tags":["fate_transport_and_sorption","soil_and_agriculture","wastewater_and_treatment"],"facet_tags":["matrix:soil_and_agriculture","matrix:wastewater"],"institution_ids":["I4210140558"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Frontiers in Materials","last_updated":"2026-11-04T10:54:05.112534","license":"cc-by","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"gold","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmats.2023.1331308","openalex_topics":["T10661","T10753","T13092"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10753","pub_date":"2024-01-11","study_type":"article","title":"Predicting environmental biodegradability using initial rates: mineralization of cellulose, guar and their semisynthetic derivatives in wastewater and soil","type":"article","work_id":"W4390743221","year":2024},{"abstract":"","author_count":7,"author_ids":["A5020840113","A5032295889","A5041563613","A5060882878","A5067823186","A5110131468","A5111722036"],"author_institution_ids":["I1312222531","I1336096307","I4210140558"],"authors":[{"id":"A5110131468","name":"Joseph P. Greene"},{"id":"A5020840113","name":"William Hart\u2010Cooper"},{"id":"A5067823186","name":"Lennard F. Torres"},{"id":"A5041563613","name":"Julia C. Cunniffe"},{"id":"A5111722036","name":"Artur K. Klamczynski"},{"id":"A5032295889","name":"Gregory M. Glenn"},{"id":"A5060882878","name":"William John Orts"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":2,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-0716-3613-8_1","domain_tags":[],"facet_tags":["matrix:marine"],"institution_ids":["I1312222531","I1336096307","I36053171","I4210140558"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Methods and protocols in food science","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-0716-3613-8_1","openalex_topics":["T10661","T10753","T13092"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10661","pub_date":"2024-01-01","study_type":"book-chapter","title":"Biodegradability of Biodegradable Plastics in Compost, Marine, and Anaerobic Environments Assessed by Automated Respirometry","type":"book-chapter","work_id":"W4391974549","year":2024},{"abstract":"High Resolution Image Download MS PowerPoint Slide Chitosans of varying molecular weights were solubilized with acids (lactic, acetic, and malic) and formed into films with glycerin added as a plasticizer, with additional treatments applied to tune the solubility and tensile properties of the films. Lactic acid solubilized chitosan made films that had a wider range of tensile properties when tuned by the glycerin concentration. Neutralizing the films led to tensile strength increasing from 16.48 to 58.95 MPa, with a loss in strain at break percent decreasing from 47.95% to 28.19%. A plasticizer bath after neutralization of a glycerin-containing film leads to an increase in tensile stress from 17.97 to 26.44 MPa. The neutralized films without a plasticizer bath show a loss from 54.94 to 42.42 MPa in 98% humidity, while the neutralized sample with plasticizer decreases from 41.10 to 8.11 MPa. Having mechanisms for tunability of the properties increases the applicability of chitosan films as sustainably produced replacements for petroleum-derived plastics in single-use packaging, textiles, and many other applications.","author_count":10,"author_ids":["A5008317231","A5020840113","A5030830572","A5032295889","A5060882878","A5062244462","A5067823186","A5087653212","A5101858744","A5111617303"],"author_institution_ids":["I1312222531","I4210140558"],"authors":[{"id":"A5062244462","name":"Kaydren Orcutt"},{"id":"A5087653212","name":"Zach McCaffrey"},{"id":"A5067823186","name":"Lennard F. Torres"},{"id":"A5008317231","name":"Delilah F. Wood"},{"id":"A5030830572","name":"Tina Williams"},{"id":"A5111617303","name":"Artur P. Klamczynski"},{"id":"A5101858744","name":"Jong Heon KIM"},{"id":"A5032295889","name":"Gregory M. Glenn"},{"id":"A5060882878","name":"William John Orts"},{"id":"A5020840113","name":"William Hart\u2010Cooper"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":4,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acssusresmgt.4c00330","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","wastewater_and_treatment"],"facet_tags":["matrix:food_and_drink"],"institution_ids":["I1312222531","I4210140558"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"ACS Sustainable Resource Management","last_updated":"2026-09-22T06:50:58.402377","license":"cc-by-nc-nd","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"hybrid","oa_url":"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/pdf/10.1021/acssusresmgt.4c00330?ref=article_openPDF","openalex_topics":["T10488","T10610","T10661"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"core","primary_topic":"T10488","pub_date":"2025-02-11","study_type":"article","title":"Bioplastics from Shellfish Waste: Tuning the Tensile and Solubility Properties of Chitosan Films","type":"article","work_id":"W4407356566","year":2025}]}
